{
  "mn49:0.1": "Middle Discourses 49 ",
  "mn49:0.2": "On the Invitation of Divinity ",
  "mn49:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn49:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn49:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn49:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn49:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn49:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn49:2.1": "“This one time, mendicants, I was staying near Ukkaṭṭhā in the Subhaga Forest at the root of a magnificent sal tree. ",
  "mn49:2.2": "Now at that time Baka the Divinity had the following harmful misconception: ",
  "mn49:2.3": "‘This is permanent, this is everlasting, this is eternal, this is whole, this is not liable to pass away. For this is where there’s no being born, growing old, dying, passing away, or being reborn. And there’s no other escape beyond this.’ ",
  "mn49:3.1": "Then I knew what Baka the Divinity was thinking. ",
  "mn49:3.2": "As easily as a strong person would extend or contract their arm, I vanished from the Subhaga Forest and reappeared in that realm of divinity. ",
  "mn49:3.3": "Baka saw me coming off in the distance ",
  "mn49:3.4": "and said, ",
  "mn49:3.5": "‘Come, good fellow! Welcome, good fellow! ",
  "mn49:3.6": "It’s been a long time since you took the opportunity to come here. ",
  "mn49:3.7": "For this is permanent, this is everlasting, this is eternal, this is whole, this is not liable to pass away. For this is w